# Secrets.
#
# Deny every env file at any depth, then let the two committed templates back
# through. Listing `server/.env` alone was one `touch .env` away from putting
# real keys in a public repo — the rule has to be the deny, not the allow.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The local database. Never the deployed one, which is not a file.
server/prisma/*.db
server/prisma/*.db-journal

